# vSphere Provider

> Analyzed from commit: `baf9c7bcc` on `2026-09-17`
> Source paths: `pkg/controller/provider/container/vsphere/`, `pkg/controller/provider/model/vsphere/`, `pkg/controller/provider/web/vsphere/`

Source: [forklift](https://github.com/kubev2v/forklift) backend — inventory collector + REST handlers run inside the **Inventory** controller.

---

## Package Purpose

The vSphere provider connects to vCenter or standalone ESXi via `govmomi`, maintains a SQLite-backed inventory mirror using vSphere's PropertyCollector (`WaitForUpdatesEx`), validates VMs asynchronously through the OPA policy agent, checks migration-required vCenter privileges, and exposes inventory over the Forklift REST API. vCenter-only features (vAPI tags, privilege checks) use a secondary REST client.

